   "text": {
    "L1": "For two numbers, HCF multiplied by LCM equals their product.",
    "L2": "The rule is not a general rule for three numbers.",
    "L3": "Take 12 and 18. Their prime factors are 2×2×3 and 2×3×3.",
    "L4": "The HCF takes the shared primes, giving 6. The LCM combines the needed primes, giving 36.",
    "L5": "So 6×36 equals 216, and 12×18 also equals 216.",
    "L6": "The rule can find a missing value. If the product is 180 and the HCF is 6, divide 180 by 6.",
    "L7": "The LCM is 30. Check that the HCF divides the LCM.",
    "L8": "Now place the missing LCM on the number line."
   },
   "narration": {
